(4016608, 570467, 30982, '<td valign="top">Love the title!  Fun pic that captures some of the atmosphere of county fairs.  Probably somewhat limited appeal to DPC voters, but what the heck - photography is a great way to share bits of culture, and this here be such a bit!</td>', 'Love the title!  Fun pic that captures some of the atmosphere of county fairs.  Probably somewhat limited appeal to DPC voters, but what the heck - photography is a great way to share bits of culture, and this here be such a bit!', '2007-08-21 05:24:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4016610, 570081, 30982, '<td valign="top">Another I think is very underappreciated, but I suspect that some DPCers never will like flowers.  I don''t know why - they''re very photogenic and usually patient models.  Love the DOF you used here, and the title ties it in very well.  Very lovely shot - you do these well!</td>', 'Another I think is very underappreciated, but I suspect that some DPCers never will like flowers.  I don''t know why - they''re very photogenic and usually patient models.  Love the DOF you used here, and the title ties it in very well.  Very lovely shot - you do these well!', '2007-08-21 05:29:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4016615, 569814, 16046, '<td valign="top">Way to go Sandy, very proud of you!</td>', 'Way to go Sandy, very proud of you!', '2007-08-21 05:42:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4016672, 569814, 41047, '<td valign="top">congratulations, sandy! outstanding portrait.</td>', 'congratulations, sandy! outstanding portrait.', '2007-08-21 06:44:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4016675, 570051, 52549, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by electrolost:</b></div><hr/><i> Don''t get me wrong this is a awesome shot. It is crisp, the colors are amazing in short it is a really good shot. but how many times can you win a ribbon with the same shot? Are people that amazed by the same thing that its a surefire thing? Have you tried other things like sand hitting glass, water from a water gun, or anything else&gt;? You have  a great talent for these macro stop motions I personally would like to see some diffrent things. Don''t get trapped doing the same thing over and over because its a automatic good score...Just some thoughts......congrats on the ribbon </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>From your point of view you are, no doubt, right.<br/>From my point of view its a different ball-game. This type of high speed photography has become a passion to me. Its an extremely difficult type of image to get which probably accounts for some of the huge interest, especially with people who have tried this sort of thing. No two images are the same  they may look similar  but theyre not the same. For me, this is another fascinating aspect of the work I put into it. And Im still learning. When I look at the first splash shots I did two years ago I find that Im now getting better results. Definitely better focus, better DOF. Im improving. This is also one of the reasons I show them here, any criticism, any comments are always a help.<br/>One thing Ive learned here is that no image is a surefire thing. No image automatically gets a good score. This is fine with me  I take what I get and learn from it.<br/> <br/>Thanks for your thoughts Robert, I appreciate it.<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by electrolost: Don''t get me wrong this is a awesome shot. It is crisp, the colors are amazing in short it is a really good shot. but how many times can you win a ribbon with the same shot? Are people that amazed by the same thing that its a surefire thing? Have you tried other things like sand hitting glass, water from a water gun, or anything else>? You have  a great talent for these macro stop motions I personally would like to see some diffrent things. Don''t get trapped doing the same thing over and over because its a automatic good score...Just some thoughts......congrats on the ribbon   From your point of view you are, no doubt, right.From my point of view its a different ball-game. This type of high speed photography has become a passion to me. Its an extremely difficult type of image to get which probably accounts for some of the huge interest, especially with people who have tried this sort of thing. No two images are the same  they may look similar  but theyre not the same. For me, this is another fascinating aspect of the work I put into it. And Im still learning. When I look at the first splash shots I did two years ago I find that Im now getting better results. Definitely better focus, better DOF. Im improving. This is also one of the reasons I show them here, any criticism, any comments are always a help.One thing Ive learned here is that no image is a surefire thing. No image automatically gets a good score. This is fine with me  I take what I get and learn from it. Thanks for your thoughts Robert, I appreciate it.', '2007-08-21 06:45:02.000000', NULL, 0),
