(4022245, 570072, 67018, '<td valign="top">I know it''s not "technically" the same photograph, but for all intensive purposes, it is.<br/> <br/>While they''re both very lovely, I don''t think they both should''ve been allowed according to the contest rules. JMO<br/> <br/>Gene</td>', 'I know it''s not "technically" the same photograph, but for all intensive purposes, it is. While they''re both very lovely, I don''t think they both should''ve been allowed according to the contest rules. JMO Gene', '2007-08-22 19:23:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4022448, 570072, 59267, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kini62:</b></div><hr/><i> I know it''s not "technically" the same photograph, but for all intensive purposes, it is.<br/> <br/>While they''re both very lovely, I don''t think they both should''ve been allowed according to the contest rules. JMO<br/> <br/>Gene </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Gene, when you go to a beautiful place. Do you release shutter only once? If not, do you release twice "purposely"?<br/>I am sorry but I am different from you. I don''t have time to consider how many shots do I need to take.<br/>My camera was on the tripod and I took 5 shots, all of them have the same composition but different clouds because they moved fast.<br/>BTW, which rule said this is not allowed? Please read the rules carefully.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-08-23 01:39:27.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by kini62: I know it''s not "technically" the same photograph, but for all intensive purposes, it is. While they''re both very lovely, I don''t think they both should''ve been allowed according to the contest rules. JMO Gene   Gene, when you go to a beautiful place. Do you release shutter only once? If not, do you release twice "purposely"?I am sorry but I am different from you. I don''t have time to consider how many shots do I need to take.My camera was on the tripod and I took 5 shots, all of them have the same composition but different clouds because they moved fast.BTW, which rule said this is not allowed? Please read the rules carefully.', '2007-08-22 21:09:55.000000', '2007-08-23 02:39:27.000000', 0),
(4022467, 570072, 67018, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by william88:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kini62:</b></div><hr/><i> I know it''s not "technically" the same photograph, but for all intensive purposes, it is.<br/> <br/>While they''re both very lovely, I don''t think they both should''ve been allowed according to the contest rules. JMO<br/> <br/>Gene </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Gene, when you go to a beautiful place. Do you release shutter only once? If not, do you release twice "purposely"?<br/>I am sorry but I am different from you. I don''t have time to consider how many shots do I need to take.<br/>My camera was on the tripod and I took 5 shots, all of them have the same composition but different clouds because they moved fast.<br/>BTW, which rule said this is not allowed? Please read the rules carefully yourself. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It would be based on this one: "use the same original image in more than one challenge."<br/> <br/>While I agree that when you are in a situation like you were that taking many photos is the thing to do, I don''t agree with using what is essentially the same photo in more than one contest. <br/> <br/>As I said you are technically correct in using this second image, I just don''t agree with it. Again JMO. <br/> <br/>Gene</td>', 'Originally posted by william88: Originally posted by kini62: I know it''s not "technically" the same photograph, but for all intensive purposes, it is. While they''re both very lovely, I don''t think they both should''ve been allowed according to the contest rules. JMO Gene   Gene, when you go to a beautiful place. Do you release shutter only once? If not, do you release twice "purposely"?I am sorry but I am different from you. I don''t have time to consider how many shots do I need to take.My camera was on the tripod and I took 5 shots, all of them have the same composition but different clouds because they moved fast.BTW, which rule said this is not allowed? Please read the rules carefully yourself.   It would be based on this one: "use the same original image in more than one challenge." While I agree that when you are in a situation like you were that taking many photos is the thing to do, I don''t agree with using what is essentially the same photo in more than one contest.  As I said you are technically correct in using this second image, I just don''t agree with it. Again JMO.  Gene', '2007-08-22 21:22:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4022475, 570072, 59267, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kini62:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by william88:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kini62:</b></div><hr/><i> I know it''s not "technically" the same photograph, but for all intensive purposes, it is.<br/> <br/>While they''re both very lovely, I don''t think they both should''ve been allowed according to the contest rules. JMO<br/> <br/>Gene </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Gene, when you go to a beautiful place. Do you release shutter only once? If not, do you release twice "purposely"?<br/>I am sorry but I am different from you. I don''t have time to consider how many shots do I need to take.<br/>My camera was on the tripod and I took 5 shots, all of them have the same composition but different clouds because they moved fast.<br/>BTW, which rule said this is not allowed? Please read the rules carefully yourself. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It would be based on this one: "use the same original image in more than one challenge."<br/>Gene </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>OPEN YOUR EYES, they are from two different original images. Why don''t you put them side by side and compare?<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-08-22 20:28:45.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by kini62: Originally posted by william88: Originally posted by kini62: I know it''s not "technically" the same photograph, but for all intensive purposes, it is. While they''re both very lovely, I don''t think they both should''ve been allowed according to the contest rules. JMO Gene   Gene, when you go to a beautiful place. Do you release shutter only once? If not, do you release twice "purposely"?I am sorry but I am different from you. I don''t have time to consider how many shots do I need to take.My camera was on the tripod and I took 5 shots, all of them have the same composition but different clouds because they moved fast.BTW, which rule said this is not allowed? Please read the rules carefully yourself.   It would be based on this one: "use the same original image in more than one challenge."Gene   OPEN YOUR EYES, they are from two different original images. Why don''t you put them side by side and compare?', '2007-08-22 21:26:08.000000', '2007-08-22 21:28:45.000000', 0),
